From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Duron27 <duron27@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 00:49:23 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] Live cells through seamless doors: the cell behind an open
 door is in the scene

The cell behind an open seamless door is loaded into the scene as a secondary cell, so NPCs there react, path to
the door and come through. The patch's door transform maps positions between the two sides.

- Scene: secondary cells (physics, mechanics, scripts, Lua; no navigator, water or ambient of their own), loaded
  one per frame while the door swings open and drawn under the portal. When the player crosses, cells are promoted
  and demoted instead of being unloaded and loaded again.
- The doorway is passable for every actor, and actors who walk past its plane move to the other side's cell.
- AiCombat, AiPursue and AiFollow go through the door (the pathgrid behind it), opening it if it is shut. A shut
  door's far cell stays loaded for up to 60 s while someone is pursuing.
- Mapped through the door: LOS (through the doorway's opening), aiming, distances, processing range, visibility,
  awareness, crime witnesses (also heard through the open door), combat engagement and sounds.
- Arrows and bolts cross the doorway.
- World::clear closes the door, so the portal works after loading a save.
- The view through the door gets water, and terrain chunks under the composite map level.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
